# Stencil context

`getCropperContext(): CropperContext` reads the nearest cropper's Svelte `createContext` value. Call it during initialization. Outside `Cropper` or `FixedCropper`, it throws a descriptive error. Nested croppers shadow the outer provider.

```ts
interface CropperContext {
	readonly cropper: CropperInstance;
	readonly disabled: boolean;
	readonly image: CropperImage | null;
	registerStencil(getOptions: () => StencilOptions): () => void;
}

interface StencilOptions {
	aspectRatio?: RawAspectRatio | (() => RawAspectRatio);
	boundingBox?: BoundingBoxType;
	[key: string]: unknown;
}

type StencilConstraints<E extends SettingsExtension = {}> = (
	settings: CropperSettingsInput<E>,
	options: Readonly<StencilOptions>
) => Partial<CropperSettingsInput<E>>;
```

`BoundingBoxType` comes from `advanced-cropper/extensions/fit-to-image`. All other types above are exported by `svelte-advanced-cropper`.

| Member | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `cropper` | Stable base API, usable during child initialization. |
| `disabled` | Reactive parent disabled getter; combine with local disabled state. |
| `image` | Reactive displayed image, or `null`. |
| `registerStencil` | Store a reactive options getter; install destruction cleanup and return idempotent early cleanup. |

Register before a state guard. One live stencil is permitted; zero is valid when children are supplied. Registration changes reconcile the current state even when ordinary automatic reconciliation is disabled. SSR registration performs no browser work.

The context intentionally has no extension generic. Use a typed snippet or explicit prop when an application control needs `CropperInstance<E>`. Boundary and source registration belong to [layer snippets](/docs/reference/snippets), not the stencil context.

The default strategy gives explicit cropper ratio settings precedence over rectangle suggestions. A circle supplies both `aspectRatio: 1` and its circular bounding box. FixedCropper uses the fixed stencil-size strategy. [Build a stencil](/docs/composition/stencil-context) shows registration and reactive reads together.
